From: Wave7 development <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: recycle RX DMA pages

Adapt Lorenzo Bianconi's October 2026 page_pool series to the
Wave7 RX ownership changes. Keep the 2048-byte device data window
separate from skb_shared_info, provide aligned headroom, and charge
the full allocation. Publish descriptor ownership only after ring
admission. Recycle the unused descriptors to an initialized list.

Retire cookie-owned buffers before destroying the pool, including
setup failure. Keep the uncommon fragment reinjection path separate
from the persistent RX mapping and correct fragment expansion size.
Use the actual partner datapath in the RX error handler.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/ath12k/20261008-ath12k-pp-v1-0-68f888cd7eec@oss.qualcomm.com/
---
